		<description><![CDATA[<p>At the halfway point of the year, according to MediaTraffic, Madonna&#8216;s Rebel Heart is the 19th worldwide best selling album [...]</p>
<p>The post <a rel="nofollow" href="http://drownedmadonna.com/rebel-heart-among-worldwide-top-20-biggest-selling-albums-of-2015/20150707">Rebel Heart among Worldwide Top 20 Biggest Selling Albums of 2015</a> appeared first on <a rel="nofollow" href="http://drownedmadonna.com">Madonna news new album Rebel Heart</a>.</p>
]]></description>
				<content:encoded><![CDATA[<p>At the halfway point of the year, according to <a href="https://www.facebook.com/permalink.php?story_fbid=892489984158521&amp;id=299303286810530" target="_blank">MediaTraffic</a>, <strong>Madonna</strong>&#8216;s <strong>Rebel Heart</strong> is the <strong>19th</strong> worldwide <strong>best selling album</strong> of 2015, so far.</p>
<p>Here&#8217;s the complete top 40:</p>
<p>01 “1989” Taylor Swift 2,944,000 sales<br />
02 “X” Ed Sheeran 2,565,000 sales<br />
03 “In The Lonely Hour” Sam Smith 2,408,000 sales<br />
04 “50 Shades Of Grey” Soundtrack 1,693,000 sales<br />
